# ByteTalk Backend Architecture Overview

## ⚡ Tech Stack
- **Runtime**: Node.js
- **Framework**: Express 5
- **Database**: MongoDB (via Mongoose)
- **Real-time**: Socket.IO
- **Security**: JWT & Bcrypt
- **Storage**: Cloudinary (for images)
- **Deployment**: Configured for Vercel

## 📁 Project Structure
```text
server/
├── controllers/  # Business logic for Auth & Messages
├── lib/          # Utilities (Mongoose connect, Cloudinary, Token utils)
├── middleware/   # Custom Express middlewares (Auth protection)
├── models/       # Mongoose Schemas (User, Message)
├── routes/       # API endpoints definitions
├── server.js     # Entry point, Socket.IO setup, Middleware registration
└── vercel.json   # Deployment configuration
```

## 🔐 Authentication Flow
1. **JWT based**: Tokens are generated in [userControllers.js](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/server/controllers/userControllers.js) and expected in the `token` header.
2. **Middleware**: [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/server/middleware/auth.js) provides [protectRoute](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/server/middleware/auth.js#4-35) which verifies the JWT and attaches the user object to `req.user`.
3. **Password Hashing**: Uses `bcrypt` with a salt factor of 10 for secure storage.

## 📡 Real-time Messaging (Socket.IO)
- **Mapped Connections**: Uses a global `useSocketMap` object in [server.js](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/server/server.js) to link `userIds` to `socketIds`.
- **Online Tracking**: Emits `getOnlineUsers` (the keys of the map) whenever a connection is established or severed.
- **Message Dispatch**: [sendMessage](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/server/controllers/messageController.js#108-139) in [messageController.js](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/server/controllers/messageController.js) looks up the recipient's `socketId` in the map and emits a `newMessage` event if they are online.

## 💾 Data Modeling
### User Schema
- Stores `fullName`, `email`, `password`, `profilePic` (URL), and `bio`.
- Uses timestamps for registration tracking.

### Message Schema
- Links `senderId` and `receiverId` (Refs to [User](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/server/controllers/messageController.js#8-36)).
- Supports both `text` and `image` (Cloudinary URL).
- Tracks [seen](file:///c:/Users/anurag.prajapati/Documents/ByteTalk/Chat%20Application/src/context/ChatContext.jsx#190-198) status (Boolean).

## 📡 API Interface
### Auth Routes
- `POST /api/auth/signUp`: Register + Image upload support.
- `POST /api/auth/login`: Authentication + JWT generation.
- `GET /api/auth/check`: Token validation.
- `PUT /api/auth/update-profile`: Profile modification (Bio, Name, Avatar).

### Message Routes
- `GET /api/messages/users`: List all users except self + unseen counts.
- `GET /api/messages/:id`: Conversation history + markings as seen.
- `POST /api/messages/send/:id`: Send text/image + Real-time emit.
- `PUT /api/messages/mark/:id`: Specific message read receipt update.
